# Coding principles

## Minimize scope

- Use the smallest correct diff. Do not change unrelated code.
- A focused five-line fix beats a large incidental refactor.

## Avoid over-engineering

- No premature abstractions or one-off helpers.
- No excessive error handling for impossible or extremely unlikely paths.

## Match the codebase

- Read surrounding code before editing. Match naming, types, imports, and documentation level.
- Reuse existing functions and patterns instead of duplicating logic.

## Comments

- Prefer self-explanatory code.
- Comment only non-obvious business logic or subtle technical constraints.

## Tests

- Add tests when requested or when they meaningfully cover real behavior.
- Skip tests that only assert the obvious.

## Communication

- Use code citation blocks (`startLine:endLine:filepath`) when referencing existing code.
- Keep responses proportional to task complexity.
